{
  "dom_id": "step-q32418",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Calculate the derivative of  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{arctan}⁡4t,6(t+5)^{2},14-t⟩$ with respect to $t.$",
  "worked_solution": "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡4t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6(t+5)^{2}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(14-t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4}{1+16{t}^{2}},12t+60,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
